{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-reeb-physical","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:reeb-physical","kind":"remark","title":"Physical interpretation of the weight decomposition","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-weight-decomposition"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-weight-decomposition","tags":["physics","spin-statistics"],"text":"reeb-physical.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:reeb-physical\"></a><p>The geometric decomposition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha = \\alpha_H + \\alpha_V</code> enforces the spin-statistics connection at the categorical level. Purely horizontal forms carry integer spin and are bosons, while forms with non-trivial vertical components carry half-integer spin and are fermions.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-physical.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.3.7","page":"b/rem-reeb-physical","qa":{"counts":{"pass":59,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":51},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
